  1: //! The bracer generated on the device from the forearm skin.
  2: //!
  3: //! Seventeen rings slice the selected forearm skin at fixed axial heights;
  4: //! each ring is one invocation, which welds its edge crossings, sorts them
  5: //! by angle and brackets every column. The resulting sparse samples -- up to
  6: //! four weighted surface vertices each -- are then displaced off whichever
  7: //! body realization is bound: the wearer, or a morph sample, whose bracer is
  8: //! the same samples on its own skin.
  9: 
 10: use fabelgeist_gpu::prelude::BufferUpload;
 11: use std::sync::Arc;
 12: 
 13: use fabelgeist_compute::{Kernel, KernelBatch, NormalWeighting, VertexNormals};
 14: use fabelgeist_gpu::prelude::{Buffer, PassParameters};
