1: //! What hair is made of: the parameters of the Chiang hair BSDF.
2: //!
3: //! DiffLocks shades its strands with Blender's Principled Hair BSDF in the
4: //! Chiang model (Chiang et al. 2016): a dielectric cylinder with cuticle
5: //! scales, its colour the absorption of the melanin in its cortex. Colour
6: //! comes from how much melanin there is and how much of it is the red
7: //! pheomelanin rather than the dark eumelanin, as Blender parameterises it,
8: //! plus an optional dye. [`HairMaterial::absorption`] is that coefficient;
9: //! [`HairMaterial::base_color`] the colour it gives a strand (Chiang's
10: //! mapping, inverted), which the real-time shading uses.
11: //!
12: //! Along the strand DiffLocks' material varies the melanin two ways, which
13: //! its metadata records: darker towards the root (`root_darkness_start`,
14: //! `_end`, `_strength`, as shares of the strand) and in waves along it
15: //! (`material_wave_scale`, `_phase_offset`, `_strength`); and it takes the
16: //! BSDF's `coat`. [`HairMaterial`] has the same, under those names.
17: 
18: use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
19: 
20: #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]
21: pub struct HairMaterial {
22:     /// 0 is white, 0.2 blond, 0.5 brown, 0.8 dark brown, 1 black.
