7: //! random per strand (`Random Offset` turns at most). The radius runs from
8: //! `Factor Start` to `Factor End` of `Radius` along the strand, and the curl
9: //! eases in over the first `Curl Start` of it (smootherstep, then square
10: //! root). A strand moves to guide point plus circle, by `Factor` -- so a
11: //! clump curls together, a guide around its own path and its strands along
12: //! with it.
13: //!
