1: //! The hair node stack.
2: //!
3: //! DiffLocks' dataset pipeline is a stack of Blender geometry nodes over a
4: //! few dozen hand-placed guide strands: interpolate them into ~100K strands
5: //! across the scalp, then clump, curl, frizz and noise them -- each several
6: //! times at different scales and strengths -- shrinkwrap them off the body,
7: //! and drape them under gravity and wind. The node groups it uses are
8: //! Blender's procedural hair assets, some in revised copies (`Interpolate
9: //! Hair Curves V2`, `Clump Hair Curves_V2`, `Create Guide Index Map`,
10: //! `Blend Hair Curves`, `Shrinkwrap Hair Curves`, `Restore Curve Segment
11: //! Length`, `Set Hair Curve Profile`).
12: //!
13: //! Each operation here is one of those groups, written out from its node
14: //! graph: the same inputs under the same names, the same fields sampled from
15: //! the same places. [`Op`] is one entry of a stack; [`crate::Groom`] runs a
16: //! stack. The operations share a few pieces the node groups share:
17: //! [`shape_range`] (the `shape_range` group every falloff goes through),
18: //! [`GuideMap`] (`Create Guide Index Map`: which strand leads each clump)
19: //! and [`restore_lengths`] (`Restore Curve Segment Length`).
20: //!
21: //! Every operation reads its input from a snapshot and writes a strand per
22: //! task, so a stack runs in parallel over strands.
